---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/base';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  breadcrumb="Cookie Policy"
  description="What this website stores in your browser, and how to change it. This site sets no cookies."
  noindex={true}>
  <section class="legal">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="sec-mark mono">Legal</p>
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="mono">Last updated: 07 August 2026</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>This website does not use cookies. It does not track you across other
      sites, it carries no advertising, and it asks you to consent to nothing,
      because nothing is stored on your device that you did not ask for.</p>
      <p>One small preference is kept in your browser, and one measurement
      script runs. Both are described below.</p>

      <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
      <p>A single value, <strong>opt-theme</strong>, held in your browser's local
      storage. It contains one word, either <strong>light</strong> or
      <strong>dark</strong>, so that the site opens in the theme you chose the
      last time you were here. It stays until you clear it.</p>
      <p>This value is created only if you use the light and dark toggle in the
      site header. It never leaves your browser, it is not sent to us or to anyone
      else, and it holds nothing that identifies you. Under the Privacy and
      Electronic Communications Regulations, storage of this kind is exempt from
      the consent requirement because it exists solely to deliver something you
      explicitly asked for.</p>

      <h2>Measurement</h2>
      <p>We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to see how many people read the site
      and which pages they read. It was chosen because it works without cookies:
      it stores no identifier on your device, places nothing there for you to
      consent to, and cannot follow you to other websites.</p>
      <p>It records the page viewed, the site you arrived from, the country the
      visit came from, the general browser and device type, and how quickly the
      page loaded. Cloudflare states that it does not follow you over time by
      your IP address, your browser's user agent or any other fixed attribute,
      and does not fingerprint your device. Visits are counted by noticing that
      a page view arrived from a different website, not by recognising you. The
      figures reach us in aggregate: we cannot identify you from them, and we
      cannot pick your visit out of them.</p>
      <p>The script is loaded from
      <strong>static.cloudflareinsights.com</strong>, which is the only external
      network call this site makes.</p>

      <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It sets no cookies of any kind.</li>
        <li>It carries no advertising, and no advertising or marketing tags.</li>
        <li>It runs no cross-site tracking, and no social media or other
        third-party tracking code.</li>
        <li>It embeds no social media buttons, videos or maps that would load
        third-party code.</li>
        <li>It loads no fonts from external networks. Fonts are served from this
        site's own domain.</li>
        <li>It builds no profile of you, and takes no automated decisions about
        you.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Managing what is stored</h2>
      <p>You can remove the theme preference at any time by clearing site data for
      optionone.io in your browser settings. Every major browser offers this,
      usually under privacy or site settings. The site will still work; it will
      simply open in its default light theme, or follow your system setting, until
      you choose again.</p>
      <p>If you block local storage entirely, the site continues to function
      normally and your theme choice is not remembered between visits.</p>
      <p>The measurement script stores nothing, so there is nothing to clear. If
      you would rather it did not run at all, any standard content blocker will
      stop it, and the site works exactly the same without it.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If cookies or any tracking technology are ever introduced to this site,
      this page will be updated and, where the law requires it, your consent will
      be asked for before anything is set. The date at the top shows when this was
      last revised.</p>

      <h2>More detail</h2>
      <p>How personal data is handled more generally is set out in our
      <a href={withBase('/legal/privacy')}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
